  },
  {
    "insert": "Dear author of this Expose, \n\nthank you for adressing this research question and I enjoyed reading your work. Here is how I understood your project proposal:\n\nYou want to use existing data from real patients (like imaging data, genomics data, etc.) to be able to construct an AI Model, that will use "
  },
  {
    "insert": "all",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " types of health data to suggest individualized treatment plans.\n\nAnd here is a selection of highlights by section:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "1.Motivation",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nGood: \nI liked your anker and abstract explanation of the problem, good job."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Research Questions are listed nicely and allow to understand the main RQ more."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "Room for improvement: \n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "It would be also nice how the problem is handled now or what is the ",
    "attributes": {
      "background": "#ffffff"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "exact gap",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true,
      "background": "#ffffff"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " in research, i.e. mention the \"State of the Art\" briefly. Your current introduction gives a very broad overview of the current situation and the problem, and for the Research Question to be evaluated properly please be more precise.",
    "attributes": {
      "background": "#ffffff"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "2.Approach:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nRoom for improvement:\nGenerally there were too much subsections and a very little information. Better to have 2-3 mandatory sections (state of the art, theoretical framework, etc.) and fill them with meaningful information, not just abstract. Quality over quantity!"
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "2.2 Theoretical Framework:",
    "attributes": {
      "underline": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " I missed the definition of privacy preserving methods."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n"
  },
  {
    "insert": "3.Schedule:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nAs the schedule is usually a personal thing, I left optional comments there, what I would do if I were you. Generally it is very good written and can be even reused (e.g. when you are writing your real thesis).\n\nFor your Expose to be complete and to have actual scientific value, consider those "
  },
  {
    "insert": "general points:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nI missed a part where you introduce the groundbreak of your research. You mentioned GANs, VAEs, federated learning, but where is the "
  },
  {
    "insert": "exact",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " approach? An exact (dummy) approach would be: \"To achieve the goal of combining multisourced data, we will use the output of GAN Models for imaging, VAE for Genomic sequence prediction, combine them into one dataset and run our "
  },
  {
    "insert": "newly developed model ",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "(which one is up to you) to retrieve exact chemoterapy with XYZ medicaction treatment plan for adenocarcinoma patients for the timescale over 6 months.\" Several "
  },
  {
    "insert": "exact ",
